  <data name="richTextBox5.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Passengers—including students, PWDs, and senior citizens—are entitled to fair treatment and may not be denied transport services due to their status. This is supported by Republic Acts No. 9994 and 7277.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="richTextBox4.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Article 1755 of the New Civil Code of the Philippines requires public utility vehicle operators to exercise extraordinary diligence in transporting passengers, ensuring their safety and comfort during travel.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="richTextBox3.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Republic Act No. 11314, the Student Fare Discount Act, grants students a 20% fare discount in PUVs during weekdays, excluding weekends and holidays. A valid school ID or proof of enrollment must be shown to claim this discount.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="richTextBox2.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Under Republic Act No. 7277 or the Magna Carta for Disabled Persons, persons with disabilities are entitled to a 20% discount on PUV fares. This applies to all land-based transport services and requires the presentation of a valid PWD ID.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="richTextBox1.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Republic Act No. 9994, also known as the Expanded Senior Citizens Act of 2010, mandates a 20% fare discount for senior citizens using public utility vehicles (PUVs). To avail of the discount, a valid Senior Citizen ID must be presented. The discount applies to all land-based public transportation including jeepneys, buses, and TNVS units like Grab.</value>
